## Recommendation: Audited Vendor Fork (hybrid, Design B's shape + Design A's dependency trim)

**Approach.** One git repo `strape`, full fork of `earendil-works/pi`, organized so ~99.9% of the tree stays byte-identical to a reviewed upstream tag. Divergence = **5 small committed hunks** in upstream files + one additive `strape/` directory. Branches: `vendor` (pristine mirror, hard-reset to tags) and `main` (vendor + hunks). Merge, never rebase; a `verify-overlay.mjs` invariant checker in CI fails loudly if a merge clobbers a hunk.

**Conflicts resolved (verified in-tree, source repo left clean):**
- **Dep trim vs runtime denylist → trim wins.** Design B called trimming "pure divergence, no runtime benefit" because SDKs are lazy-loaded. Half right: lazy loading (`packages/ai/src/providers/anthropic.ts:1` → `*.lazy.ts`) means no startup execution, but 87 extra packages still land on disk and in the review surface, and `protobufjs`'s install script still ships. I ran upstream's own generator: moving 5 SDKs to `devDependencies` takes the shipped closure **143 → 56 packages** and install-script packages **2 → 0**. Requires also emptying `allowedInstallScriptPackages` in both generator scripts (they hard-fail on a stale allowlist).
- **Design A's fear that trims force lockfile regeneration → false.** `npm ci --ignore-scripts --dry-run` succeeds against the untouched lockfile with both the dep trim and the workspaces trim applied (319 vs 339 pkgs; `ssh2`/`cpu-features` gone). So the two biggest wins are conflict-free forever.
- **Design A's build-time codemod overlay → rejected.** Trades 5 stable hunks for ~180 lines of string-anchor machinery with the same failure mode (upstream rewording) plus a dirty-tree build ritual. Its good ideas (invariant asserts, reviewed-deps gate) are kept.
- **No settings/env override exists** for config dir (`config.ts:491` sole definition) or context-file precedence — so a wrapper-only, fork-free rename is impossible (`getPackageDir()` walks from the coding-agent module's own `__dirname`, `config.ts:367-388`).

**Rename: yes.** ~7 lines. `piConfig {name, configDir}` + `bin` in `packages/coding-agent/package.json` (upstream-designed seam, `config.ts:487-496`) auto-derives APP_NAME/APP_TITLE/`.strape`/`~/.strape/agent`/`STRAPE_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. Plus 2 identity strings in `system-prompt.ts:121` — the one place the rename changes behavior, not cosmetics. Do **not** rename the npm scope (~469 files, zero value) or the literal `PI_*` env vars (`main.ts:572-575`).

**Claude compat: works today, zero source changes.** Project `CLAUDE.md` already a candidate (`resource-loader.ts:71`). `.claude/skills` = one settings key per scope; I confirmed the bases in code (`package-manager.ts:903-904`: project settings resolve against `<cwd>/.strape`, so `../.claude/skills` is correct as documented). Global `CLAUDE.md` needs one symlink. Never set `configDir: ".claude"` — `settings-manager.ts:201` would collide with Claude Code's own project settings file.

**Six key security measures:** (1) the 143→56 / 2→0 trim; (2) `reviewed-deps.json` gate — build fails on any `name@version`+sha512 not human-reviewed; (3) emptied install-script allowlist, so any new lifecycle-script dep hard-fails and *forces* review; (4) `high-scrutiny.json` for the class no scanner catches — `grok-mermaid@0.2.2` (created 2026-07-28, single maintainer, ~1.2k dl/mo, static import in the TUI so undenylistable); (5) vendored `packages/ai/src/providers/data/` — removes models.dev/OpenRouter fetches from every build, makes catalog changes a git diff; (6) explicit offline posture via launcher (`PI_OFFLINE=1`, `PI_SKIP_VERSION_CHECK=1`) killing all three pi.dev endpoints, plus `osv-scanner` (hash-pinned) and `npm audit signatures` against a real install (lockfile-only mode cannot verify signatures).

**Effort:** ~5-6 person-days to a trusted first build, of which 3-4 days is the irreducible review (~70k LOC after exclusions + a 47-package effective closure). Then 30-60 min per adopted release, monthly cadence ≈ 2-4 h/month.

**Proposal:** `<workspace>/strape-proposal.md` (589 lines, all 10 requested sections).